  (text "Power flags: GND, VBUS (USB-C), CELL1 / CELL2 (holders), BAT (through the cell FETs), VSYS (through D2)" (at 350.52 312.42 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top))
    (uuid a3de7939-98ff-55b0-a798-790212ba71a3)
  )
  (text "Pico pin map v2 (GP -> net)\nGP0  SPARE\nGP1  SPARE\nGP2  MOTOR_EN\nGP3  BOOST_EN\nGP4  CHG_STAT\nGP5  CHG_PG\nGP6  ENC1_A\nGP7  ENC1_B\nGP8  M1_IN1\nGP9  M1_IN2\nGP10 IMU_RST\nGP11 IMU_INT\nGP12 SPI1_MISO\nGP13 SPI1_CS\nGP14 SPI1_SCK\nGP15 SPI1_MOSI\nGP16 ENC2_A\nGP17 ENC2_B\nGP18 SPARE\nGP19 USER_LED\nGP20 M2_IN1\nGP21 M2_IN2\nGP22 IMU_WAKE\nGP26 M1_ISENSE\nGP27 M2_ISENSE\nGP28 VBAT_SENSE" (at 470 300 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top))
    (uuid 1e93a464-1de9-5347-96aa-abbaa4502a4b)
  )
  (text "Operating modes: the robot is not driven while charging (switch off). If power is left on, firmware drops\nMOTOR_EN and BOOST_EN, puts the BNO086 to sleep and sends the Pico dormant. TPS22810 UVLO is the backstop.\nUVLO options: R21 0R = internal 2.54 / 2.41 V; R21 156k + R22 100k + R23 1.27M = 3.30 / 2.70 V.\nDNP: TH1, R22, R23, R24.  Design doc: docs/PicoBalancer_Hardware_Design.pdf" (at 20 395 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5)) (justify left top))
    (uuid 37b8d0cf-5947-5306-8c9a-ba37b2b6b150)
  )

